`embInf` is the stage embedding as a Scott map, using preservation of directed suprema from [embInfFun](1972_embInfFun.md). `embInf_succ` is the recursion \(i_{n\infty} = i_{(n+1)\infty} \circ i_n\). `embInf_le_succ` and `embInf_family_directed` say that the embeddings of the coordinates of a thread form a monotone, hence directed, family. The application formula \(\bigsqcup_n i_{n\infty}(x_{n+1}(y_n))\) uses these embeddings and is [the application](1972_Application.md). **Theorem:** yes — the stage embedding into the limit and the recursion are formalized. **Proof:** partial — the recursion and the directedness of the family are proved. The application formula is not this argument.
